From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: the screen saver's weather (Open-Meteo, off until
 turned on), and the Pictures slideshow for every account

The screen saver's weather on ChromeOS comes from Google's servers, with
the user's Google account (Backdrop: Google's own builds only), so on
NickelOS there was none. Now it's the user's choice, off until turned on:
Wallpaper and style > Screen saver > Weather > "Show the weather".

- Where: beaconDB's position for the request's internet address (an empty
  request: no Wi-Fi or other data; about a city, enough for the weather),
  at most once an hour. The weather there: Open-Meteo's current
  temperature and conditions, for the place rounded to about a kilometre,
  at most every 15 minutes, and only while the screen saver shows
  (AmbientWeatherController's refresher, now also in the slideshow of a
  folder's pictures). Both free, without keys or accounts.
  AmbientClient::FetchNickelWeather (AmbientClientImpl) does both;
  NickelAmbientBackendController asks it only while the user's pref
  (nickel.screen_saver.weather) is on.
- ChromeOS's location switch still decides: AmbientWeatherController asks
  only while Privacy controls allow the location for the system, and the
  page shows ChromeOS's notice with its button when they don't.
- The icon: drawn from the system's emoji font for the WMO weather code
  ("nickel-weather:<kind>"), nothing downloaded. No weather (off, or none
  to be had): none shown, rather than the last.
- The unit: the page's Fahrenheit/Celsius (nickel.screen_saver.celsius),
  kept now (it lived for the session); Fahrenheit where the language is
  American English, else Celsius.
- The page: the switch on top of the Weather section, with where the
  weather comes from; the unit and the location notice while it's on
  (personalization_app.mojom: SetNickelWeatherEnabled,
  OnNickelWeatherEnabledChanged).

Every account's screen saver is now the Pictures folder's slideshow,
Google accounts' too: NickelOS's Chrome has none of Google's screen saver
backend, so a Google account's Google Photos and Art gallery came up
empty, and picking Feel the Breeze or Float on By (whose Google-internal
animations Chromium builds as a stub that stops the session) would have
ended the session. Guests, kiosks and public sessions have no screen
saver, as before. The Google account checks go.

